  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Alkene hydrogenation is the syn-addition of hydrogen to an alkene, saturating the bond.</p><p>A compound capable of optical rotation is said to be optically active. For a compound to be optically active, it should contain chiral carbon.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/image33-644e961d-08fc-4186-b03a-0415c204b6e6.jpg\"/><br ><br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/image34-67c7f583-f5b9-4898-8129-2a2b1edb00ed.jpg\"/></p>",
